<%# Armand's layout: the example pets and the prizes over the old desktop's
    sky, the requirements under the prizes, what to do now, whose button
    goes to the guide, and then the FAQ. Each box is a window in the old
    desktop's chrome, with its file name and an X in the title bar. The
    bar is only a picture: its X closes nothing, so it hides from screen
    readers and takes no clicks. The sponsor's name shows without
    scrolling, as Hack Club's YSWS website requirements ask. %>
<% content_for :no_topbar, true %>
<% content_for :body_class, "home-page" %>
<div class="home-sky">
  <a class="home-flag" href="https://hackclub.com" aria-label="Hack Club"><%= image_tag "landing/hack-club-flag-2026.svg", alt: "" %></a>
  <p class="home-sponsor">sponsored by <%= link_to "Armand", ApplicationHelper::SPONSOR_URL, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %></p>
  <h1 class="home-logo"><%= image_tag "landing/logo.png", alt: "Hack Club playground" %></h1>

  <h2 class="home-say" id="pets-title">Make a cool desktop pet like these</h2>
  <section class="home-window home-pets" aria-labelledby="pets-title">
    <div class="home-titlebar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="home-title">examples</span><span class="home-x">X</span></div>
    <ul class="home-pane home-examples">
      <li><a href="https://samperson.itch.io/desktop-goose" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= image_tag "landing/desktopgoose.gif", alt: "" %><span>desktop goose by samperson</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://jonasmack.itch.io/desktop-garden" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= image_tag "landing/desktopgarden.png", alt: "" %><span>desktop garden by jonasmack</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://sharyap.itch.io/frog-pond" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= image_tag "landing/frogpond.png", alt: "" %><span>frog pond by sharyap</span></a></li>
      <li><a href="https://hempuli.itch.io/baba-friend" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><%= image_tag "landing/babafriend.gif", alt: "" %><span>baba friend by hempuli</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2 class="home-say" id="merch-title">Get cool merch like this</h2>
  <section class="home-window home-prizes" aria-labelledby="merch-title">
    <div class="home-titlebar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="home-title">prizes.txt</span><span class="home-x">X</span></div>
    <div class="home-pane">
      <ul class="home-goals">
        <li><p>Spend 2 hours on your project, get a sticker sheet</p><%= image_tag "landing/stickysheet.png", alt: "a sticker sheet" %></li>
        <li><p>5 hours<br>custom keychain</p><%= image_tag "landing/keychain.png", alt: "a keychain" %></li>
        <li><p>10 hours<br>a shirt with yours, and everyone else's pet on it</p><%= image_tag "landing/shirt.png", alt: "a shirt" %></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="home-requirements">to earn merch, your pet has to meet the <%= link_to "submission requirements ↗", requirements_path, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<section class="home-window home-now" aria-labelledby="now-title">
  <div class="home-titlebar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="home-title">start.exe</span><span class="home-x">X</span></div>
  <div class="home-pane">
    <h2 id="now-title">What do I do now?</h2>
    <ol class="home-steps">
      <li><span class="step-node"><span class="step-number">1</span></span><span>follow the guide to make your pet</span></li>
      <li><span class="step-node"><span class="step-number">2</span></span><span>make it your own</span></li>
      <li><span class="step-node"><span class="step-number">3</span></span><span>ship it</span></li>
      <li><span class="step-node"><span class="step-number">4</span></span><span>get your merch</span></li>
    </ol>
    <%= link_to current_user ? "continue the guide →" : "start the guide →", guide_path, class: "btn primary big home-go" %>
  </div>
</section>

<%# The old playground's questions, from welcome.txt, in its words. What
    you get is the prizes above, and the examples are at the top. %>
<section class="home-window home-faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="home-titlebar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="home-title">faq.txt</span><span class="home-x">X</span></div>
  <div class="home-pane">
    <h2 id="faq-title">FAQ</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>what is a desktop pet?</summary>
      <p>a small program that lives on your desktop, like a character that walks around, reacts to you, or sits on your windows.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>what counts?</summary>
      <p>a cool desktop pet!! it can be anything you want, as long as it's a desktop pet! it can be a widget, a screensaver, an app, or even a website! just make sure it's something that can be easily shared and used by others! (also no AI generated pets, we want to see your creativity!!)</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>i dont know what to make</summary>
      <p>check out the cool desktop pets at the top of this page!!</p>
    </details>
    <%# An account made before the new site was the default knew the old
        desktop, which is still here (NewSite::LAUNCHED_ON). %>
    <% if knew_the_desktop? %>
      <details>
        <summary>where did the desktop go?</summary>
        <p>it's still here! <%= link_to "open the old desktop →", classic_path, aria: { haspopup: "dialog" },
                                         data: { controller: "classic-switch", action: "classic-switch#open" } %></p>
      </details>
    <% end %>
    <details>
      <summary>i have more questions :(</summary>
      <p>join <a href="https://hackclub.slack.com/archives/C0ASBTMS82H" target="_blank" rel="noopener">#playground</a> on the Hack Club Slack, where teen makers chat!! or ask @froppii there!!</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
